{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"1947 Verified -1: REAL BUG IN MY OWN TEST, not a flake - failed identically on py3.11/3.12/3.13. My held-out edge test used 'from tests.unit.test_measurement_provenance_criterion import ...'; tests.-rooted imports resolve only when the repo root is on sys.path, which 'python -m pytest' provides but the BARE pytest console script used by make test and CI does not. All my local verification had used python -m pytest, masking it. The repo has a dedicated guard for this convention (test_tests_import_convention.py) which failed alongside and named the fix. Reproduced deterministically with bare pytest, fixed to bare-name imports, scanned the whole stack for the same pattern (none), re-verified 80 passed under BARE pytest + lint clean. Fixed via fixup+autosquash into S4; had to reattach the branch after the rebase left a detached HEAD (leftover from my earlier bad rebase --onto). Rebased onto current origin/main and re-pushed 1946/1947/1948. LESSON: verify with bare pytest, matching CI."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787207881008383001,"uuid":"856ee14c-0e37-4661-9d46-3cec2ac4f966"}